WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.012 --> 00:00:17.300
After work Ally rushed home to tell Mateo her worries about Tina.

2
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:22.943
"Maybe it's another misunderstanding, like with Melanie," Mateo said.

3
00:00:22.963 --> 00:00:26.645
"Maybe." Ally started pacing.

4
00:00:26.665 --> 00:00:31.388
"I can't think straight knowing there's a Jorgandian in Sandville!"

5
00:00:32.624 --> 00:00:35.946
"Alpha, have you found any more clues about the Jorgandian?"

6
00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:37.087
Mateo asked.

7
00:00:37.107 --> 00:00:42.451
"I have scanned approximately 234 life-forms," Alpha said.

8
00:00:43.411 --> 00:00:44.552
She printed out a list.

9
00:00:47.114 --> 00:00:54.039
Ally recognized lots of names, including the mayor, employees at Pepe's, and many of Ray's regular customers.

10
00:00:54.059 --> 00:01:01.864
"But, Alpha, there are a lot more than 234 people in Sandville," Mateo said.

11
00:01:02.944 --> 00:01:04.245
"Have you scanned Tina?"

12
00:01:04.665 --> 00:01:05.286
Ally asked.

13
00:01:05.306 --> 00:01:10.089
"She's that new security guard at the museum, and she seems suspicious."

14
00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:15.213
"Negative. The museum is too far for my limited scanning ability."

15
00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:18.476
"Please try harder," Ally said.

16
00:01:18.496 --> 00:01:20.157
"This is important!"

17
00:01:21.618 --> 00:01:22.539
Alpha looked annoyed.

18
00:01:22.559 --> 00:01:25.761
"Have you tried to read this life-form's mind?"

19
00:01:25.781 --> 00:01:29.784
"Uh no," Ally said.

20
00:01:30.524 --> 00:01:34.186
"I didn't think of her as a suspect until after she left the diner."

21
00:01:34.206 --> 00:01:36.807
"Hmpf!" Alpha snorted.

22
00:01:36.827 --> 00:01:39.088
"Try harder, Allyzooba!"

23
00:01:39.108 --> 00:01:42.429
"I'm not a computer," Ally snapped.

24
00:01:43.089 --> 00:01:47.371
"And—" "We're all on the same team," Mateo interrupted.

25
00:01:47.391 --> 00:01:52.393
"Alpha, how accurate would your scans be if someone was in close range?"

26
00:01:53.773 --> 00:01:55.374
"One hundred percent accuracy."

27
00:01:57.135 --> 00:02:00.913
"It's too bad Alpha's not in a phone anymore," Mateo said.

28
00:02:00.933 --> 00:02:06.257
"Then you could bring her into town with you, Ally, and she could scan lots of people."

29
00:02:06.277 --> 00:02:11.621
"That is too bad Ally got an idea.

30
00:02:11.641 --> 00:02:13.623
"I can still do that!

31
00:02:14.764 --> 00:02:16.505
Did Ray buy a new computer yet?"

32
00:02:16.525 --> 00:02:19.848
"Nope," Mateo said.

33
00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:22.170
"Then let's use Alpha!

34
00:02:23.411 --> 00:02:26.113
I'll tell him he can borrow mine until he buys one.

35
00:02:26.854 --> 00:02:29.056
That way Alpha can scan more people."

36
00:02:30.332 --> 00:02:31.232
"Are you sure?"

37
00:02:31.653 --> 00:02:32.433
Mateo asked.

38
00:02:33.093 --> 00:02:35.094
"She still glitches sometimes."

39
00:02:36.014 --> 00:02:37.295
Alpha's screen flashed.

40
00:02:37.315 --> 00:02:40.916
"That is because I'm trapped in this primitive Earthling machine.

41
00:02:41.737 --> 00:02:44.138
But, Allyzooba, you have a valid idea.

42
00:02:44.918 --> 00:02:48.980
If you bring me to Ray's, I will be able to scan all customers in the diner.

43
00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:52.621
I can also scan all life-forms in the general vicinity."

44
00:02:55.042 --> 00:02:57.123
Ally beamed, and so did Mateo.

45
00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:59.204
"Great!" he said.

46
00:02:59.884 --> 00:03:02.546
"I'll tell Papi to hold off on buying a new computer.

47
00:03:03.106 --> 00:03:05.368
We can bring Alpha to the diner tomorrow."

48
00:03:09.791 --> 00:03:13.434
The next morning Ally and Mateo set up Alpha in Ray's office.

49
00:03:17.296 --> 00:03:19.238
for lending me your computer," Ray said.

50
00:03:19.258 --> 00:03:22.019
"It will be a good test to see if I need to buy a new one."

51
00:03:22.039 --> 00:03:26.182
"We can show you how it works, Papi," Mateo said.

52
00:03:26.202 --> 00:03:28.304
"Maybe later," Ray said.

53
00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.621
"I need to get ready for my meeting with the CEO of Big City Foods.

54
00:03:32.522 --> 00:03:33.762
I want to make him a special meal."

55
00:03:35.363 --> 00:03:39.244
Ally waited for Ray to go into the kitchen, then she spoke to Alpha.

56
00:03:40.125 --> 00:03:41.445
"Now remember, Alpha.

57
00:03:41.905 --> 00:03:44.667
If you find a Jorgandian, chime once.

58
00:03:45.347 --> 00:03:46.908
But no talking while you're here.

59
00:03:47.588 --> 00:03:48.928
None. Understood?"

60
00:03:50.189 --> 00:03:51.229
Alpha didn't reply.

61
00:03:51.249 --> 00:03:53.450
"Alpha, did you hear me?"

62
00:03:53.911 --> 00:03:54.591
Ally repeated.

63
00:03:55.551 --> 00:03:57.192
Again Alpha did not respond.

64
00:03:58.192 --> 00:03:59.232
Ally rolled her eyes.

65
00:04:00.393 --> 00:04:03.373
"You can speak now, so I know you're working."

66
00:04:03.393 --> 00:04:05.994
"Of course, I'm working!"

67
00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:09.195
Alpha said just as Flo came into the office.

68
00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:14.617
"Wow!" Flo laughed when she saw the computer.

69
00:04:15.537 --> 00:04:18.998
"I can't believe Ray is joining the twenty-first century.

70
00:04:19.018 --> 00:04:22.199
I thought he'd never get a new computer!"

71
00:04:22.219 --> 00:04:28.136
"He's thinking about buying a new one, so Ally loaned hers to him," Mateo said.

72
00:04:28.156 --> 00:04:31.598
"Hello!" Phil called from the dining room.

73
00:04:31.618 --> 00:04:33.019
"Anybody here?"

74
00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:36.721
They all hurried back into the dining room.

75
00:04:36.741 --> 00:04:40.964
"Hi, Phil," Ally said nervously.

76
00:04:40.984 --> 00:04:43.605
"Uh where's Tina?"

77
00:04:43.625 --> 00:04:46.006
"She's meeting with Dr.

78
00:04:46.046 --> 00:04:47.807
Lloyd in his lab," Phil said.

79
00:04:47.827 --> 00:04:49.989
"He's telling her about his research."

80
00:04:51.289 --> 00:04:53.250
"Oh right," Ally said.

81
00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:54.651
"She mentioned that.

82
00:04:56.332 --> 00:04:58.133
Do you think she'll be in later?"

83
00:04:59.513 --> 00:05:00.193
Phil shrugged.

84
00:05:00.213 --> 00:05:04.574
"Maybe." Ally and Mateo exchanged uneasy looks.

85
00:05:06.535 --> 00:05:09.996
They needed Tina to come into the diner today so Alpha could scan her.

86
00:05:12.616 --> 00:05:14.137
Suddenly Mateo grinned.

87
00:05:14.937 --> 00:05:15.537
"Oh, Phil!

88
00:05:15.937 --> 00:05:18.598
You should tell Tina about our new policy at Ray's.

89
00:05:19.518 --> 00:05:22.499
We offer a free lunch to new residents of Sandville."

90
00:05:23.839 --> 00:05:25.520
"Ooh!" Phil said.

91
00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:27.253
"I'll send her in at lunchtime.

92
00:05:27.894 --> 00:05:29.415
Now can I give you my breakfast order?"

93
00:05:31.657 --> 00:05:34.519
While Flo took his order, Mateo gestured to Ally.

94
00:05:39.083 --> 00:05:41.385
come back at lunchtime," he whispered.

95
00:05:41.405 --> 00:05:43.867
"In case you—" Ping!

96
00:05:45.488 --> 00:05:46.829
Mateo looked at his phone.

97
00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:48.871
"It's a text from Coach.

98
00:05:49.731 --> 00:05:52.794
He needs me to take over a camp session for the little kids.

99
00:05:53.514 --> 00:05:55.116
There's something going on with his brother.

100
00:05:56.248 --> 00:05:58.933
They never argue, but they just had a big fight.

101
00:05:59.554 --> 00:06:02.138
Coach is going to the copy shop to smooth things over."
